From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lemelson <97357844+Lemelson@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 15:07:20 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] clock: keep the pause date across a reset while paused

vlc_clock_main_reset() clears pause_date even when the main clock is
still paused. vlc_clock_main_ChangePause(false) then takes the
"Reset was called before resume from Pause" early return and does not
shift first_pcr, start_time and wait_sync_ref by the pause length.

With a paused seek (decoder and es_out patches of this series), the
clock is reset and new references are created while still paused. On
resume they are not shifted by the pause. Normal resume then failed on
both the software and the VideoToolbox/AUHAL pipelines. LLDB shows
pause_date cleared by the reset while main_clock->paused is true, then,
after an 8.93 s pause, ChangePause(false) returning before the shift.

Keep pause_date across a reset (and SetFirstPcr) while the main clock
is paused. The unpaused reset behaviour and the clock lock are
unchanged.

Note for review: this deliberately reverses the upstream intent stated
in vlc_clock_main_ChangePause() (skip the shift when the stream was
paused then seeked). It is only correct together with the next clock
patch, which creates the references made while paused on the pause
origin, so they are shifted exactly once. If upstream fixes the paused
seek differently, this patch should be dropped.

Test: redesign/patches/engine/tests/test-clock-pause-reset.sh (13
cases on the public clock API; 7 fail on the unpatched clock.c).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/clock/clock.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/clock/clock.c b/src/clock/clock.c
index bb137d6..0c87e54 100644
--- a/src/clock/clock.c
+++ b/src/clock/clock.c
@@ -394,7 +394,10 @@ static void vlc_clock_main_reset(vlc_clock_main_t *main_clock)
     AvgResetAndFill(&main_clock->coeff_avg, ctx->coeff);
 
     main_clock->wait_sync_ref_priority = UINT_MAX;
-    main_clock->pause_date = VLC_TICK_INVALID;
+    /* Paused seek buffering still uses this origin. Resume must shift the
+     * new clock references by the elapsed pause, just like the input clock. */
+    if (!main_clock->paused)
+        main_clock->pause_date = VLC_TICK_INVALID;
     vlc_cond_broadcast(&main_clock->cond);
 }
 
